From 04f1697a34da7477e8205ba0b3a361b397929940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:52:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] LayerStatePermissions: fix READ_FRAME_BUFFER key type

The earlier revert of "Avoid string allocations when checking for
permissions" changed mPermissionMap from
std::vector<std::pair<String16, int>> to
std::unordered_map<std::string, int>, but missed updating the last
entry, which still constructed its key with String16(...) instead of a
plain string literal. std::string has no implicit conversion from
String16, so this failed to compile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Iffd4170b73404551c07668480cbfe51a92f75908
---
 libs/gui/LayerStatePermissions.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/gui/LayerStatePermissions.cpp b/libs/gui/LayerStatePermissions.cpp
index 33ac420ac5..ac83b454d2 100644
--- a/libs/gui/LayerStatePermissions.cpp
+++ b/libs/gui/LayerStatePermissions.cpp
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ std::unordered_map<std::string, int> LayerStatePermissions::mPermissionMap = {
          layer_state_t::Permission::ROTATE_SURFACE_FLINGER},
         {"android.permission.INTERNAL_SYSTEM_WINDOW",
          layer_state_t::Permission::INTERNAL_SYSTEM_WINDOW},
-        {String16("android.permission.READ_FRAME_BUFFER"),
+        {"android.permission.READ_FRAME_BUFFER",
          layer_state_t::Permission::READ_FRAME_BUFFER},
 };
 
